<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grand Port</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mahébourg Bay</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grand Port is a large bay and harbour on the south-east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritius">Mauritius</a>, on which the town of Mahébourg now stands. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> built its first settlement, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-frederik-hendrik">Fort Frederik Hendrik</a>, there in 1638. In August 1810 a French squadron defeated a British force in the Battle of Grand Port, the only French naval victory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a> commemorated on the Arc de Triomphe, months before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> took the island.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grand-port.jpg" alt="Grand Port" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hansueli Krapf This file was uploaded with Commonist. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2011-06-25_13-35-51_Mauritius_Grand_Port_Rose_Belle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
